WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.300
Paper mode: live prices, simulated trades.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.500
The landing page.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.900
The engine burns $ASH, and the bell rings once.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.520
Nothing rings unless it actually burned.

5
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.450
The tape: every claim, trade and burn.

6
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.300
Click a burn for its receipt.

7
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.600
Live figures, each with the time it was read.

8
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.900
Positions, pooled per market, and the activity feed.

9
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.650
Every token, with the engine’s call. Opening Silicon Frog.

10
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.850
Burned supply, and the engine right now.

11
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.750
Launching a token: four steps.

12
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.600
Step 1: choose a launchpad.

13
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.510
Only one field differs from a normal launch. Pons is picked.

14
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.900
Step 2: the stock it goes long on: Nvidia.

15
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.990
Keeping the Balanced strategy.

16
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.170
Step 3: the Bellwether wallet.

17
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.250
Copying its address.

18
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.990
On Pons: the create form, then Advanced. Nothing is submitted here.

19
00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:52.900
Pasting it into Creator wallet.

20
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.550
Back on Bellwether.

21
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.640
Step 4: the address of a real Pons token.

22
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.400
Five checks pass, including where the fees go.

23
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.300
The plan for $FILL. Then “Ring the opening bell”.

24
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.100
$FILL is registered; the bell rings for it.

25
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.800
Proof: the ledger against the wallets. The books balance.

26
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.430
Always copy the wallet address from the launch page.
